1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:07,056
Part six: Numbers to Track. This is the last section of the initial assessment.

2
00:00:07,256 --> 00:00:14,177
You record three numbers for the patient, copied from PointClickCare. Then you finalize the assessment.

3
00:00:16,077 --> 00:00:20,989
You track the same three numbers for every patient, whatever their condition:

4
00:00:21,029 --> 00:00:24,294
weight, blood pressure, and hemoglobin A1C.

5
00:00:24,594 --> 00:00:30,854
Weight and blood pressure are vitals. Copy the latest value of each, with the date it was taken.

6
00:00:31,154 --> 00:00:35,792
The A1C is a lab result. Look for it in three places, in this order:

7
00:00:35,832 --> 00:00:40,804
the Results tab, the lab reports in Misc, and the progress notes.

8
00:00:41,104 --> 00:00:44,249
If there's no A1C anywhere, don't add one.

9
00:00:46,256 --> 00:00:49,679
In the assessment menu, open Numbers to Track.

10
00:00:49,929 --> 00:00:54,461
It has two parts: vitals to track, and lab results to track.

11
00:00:55,782 --> 00:01:00,074
Under vitals, check Weight. Today's date fills in next to it.

12
00:01:00,329 --> 00:01:02,396
Check Blood Pressure too.

13
00:01:02,652 --> 00:01:06,779
Then scroll down to the lab results, and check HgbA1C.

14
00:01:07,029 --> 00:01:12,073
Those are the three numbers. Next, find their values in PointClickCare.

15
00:01:14,049 --> 00:01:18,154
In PointClickCare, scroll to the top of the patient's page.

16
00:01:18,416 --> 00:01:22,798
The banner shows the latest vitals, each with the date it was taken.

17
00:01:23,049 --> 00:01:28,819
The latest blood pressure is 142/92, taken on October 8.

18
00:01:29,082 --> 00:01:33,175
The latest weight is 206 pounds, from the same day.

19
00:01:33,432 --> 00:01:36,471
Click a vital to see its history as a chart.

20
00:01:38,116 --> 00:01:41,901
Back in ThoroughCare, type the weight: 206.

21
00:01:44,016 --> 00:01:50,105
Its date filled in as today, October 8. That matches PointClickCare, so keep it.

22
00:01:50,355 --> 00:01:55,271
In Blood Pressure, type the top number, 142, in systolic.

23
00:01:55,521 --> 00:01:58,257
Then the bottom number in diastolic.

24
00:02:00,416 --> 00:02:05,055
Check every value against PointClickCare before you move on.

25
00:02:05,095 --> 00:02:10,196
PointClickCare shows 92, so diastolic should be 92, not 88.

26
00:02:10,446 --> 00:02:15,276
The blood pressure was taken on the same day, so its date stays as it is.

27
00:02:16,582 --> 00:02:20,197
HgbA1C is checked, but it still needs a value.

28
00:02:20,462 --> 00:02:23,842
In PointClickCare, start with the Results tab.

29
00:02:24,092 --> 00:02:30,075
It lists the patient's lab results. For this patient, it's empty: No Reports Found.

30
00:02:30,325 --> 00:02:35,796
That's not a problem. Lab reports are often uploaded as documents instead.

31
00:02:43,971 --> 00:02:51,042
Next, open the Misc tab. It holds the documents uploaded to the patient's chart, sorted by category.

32
00:02:51,292 --> 00:02:54,160
Press Ctrl + F, and search for lab.

33
00:02:56,316 --> 00:03:00,976
Under Laboratory, you'll find the patient's lab reports, newest first.

34
00:03:07,179 --> 00:03:11,818
Open them one by one, and look for a hemoglobin A1C value.

35
00:03:17,816 --> 00:03:22,732
This report shows a chemistry panel and a blood count. There's no A1C.

36
00:03:24,816 --> 00:03:28,132
Check every page of the report before you move on.

37
00:03:33,416 --> 00:03:36,360
The next report has no A1C either.

38
00:03:46,598 --> 00:03:51,279
Skip reports that can't include an A1C, such as a urine culture.

39
00:04:00,382 --> 00:04:05,511
This one also has a blood count and a metabolic panel, but no A1C.

40
00:04:08,416 --> 00:04:14,441
Keep checking the reports until you find an A1C. If there isn't one anywhere, don't add it.

41
00:04:16,416 --> 00:04:20,197
Here, neither the results nor the lab reports have an A1C.

42
00:04:20,237 --> 00:04:23,636
So check the last place: the progress notes.

43
00:04:23,886 --> 00:04:28,024
They hold the details of every visit, including lab values.

44
00:04:28,274 --> 00:04:30,417
Click the Prog Notes tab.

45
00:04:31,516 --> 00:04:34,981
The patient's progress notes open, newest first.

46
00:04:41,910 --> 00:04:43,679
Then click View All.

47
00:04:44,819 --> 00:04:50,311
View All lists notes from a short time period only. To cover more, click Custom.

48
00:04:50,908 --> 00:04:53,008
Check Effective Date Range.

49
00:04:53,653 --> 00:04:58,441
Set the start date one year back, here 10/7/2025.

50
00:04:58,691 --> 00:05:00,919
Keep today as the end date.

51
00:05:01,169 --> 00:05:02,821
Then click Save.

52
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:14,328
Now the notes from the past year are listed. Press Ctrl + F, and search for A1C.

53
00:05:16,082 --> 00:05:23,665
The first match is A1C q3m: a plan to check the A1C every three months. That's not a result.

54
00:05:23,916 --> 00:05:29,161
Go to the next match. A hospital summary mentions HbA1c 7.0%,

55
00:05:29,201 --> 00:05:32,907
but without the date it was measured.

56
00:05:38,816 --> 00:05:48,020
Keep going. This match has both a value and a date: Glyco HbA1c (07/04/2026): 7.0.

57
00:05:48,270 --> 00:05:51,952
That's what you need: the value, and the date it was measured.

58
00:05:53,288 --> 00:05:57,729
Back in ThoroughCare, type the A1C value: 7.0.

59
00:05:57,979 --> 00:06:02,212
Its date filled in as today. Change it to the date it was measured.

60
00:06:02,462 --> 00:06:06,887
Use the calendar's arrows to go back to July, and pick the fourth.

61
00:06:07,137 --> 00:06:10,858
The date now reads 07/04/2026.

62
00:06:12,382 --> 00:06:16,850
That's all three numbers, and every section of the initial assessment.

63
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:23,040
To finish, click Finalize Incomplete. This marks the initial assessment as complete.

64
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:26,464
Let's recap.

65
00:06:26,664 --> 00:06:31,729
Open Numbers to Track, and check Weight, Blood Pressure, and HgbA1C.

66
00:06:31,929 --> 00:06:36,187
Copy the latest weight and blood pressure from the banner in PointClickCare,

67
00:06:36,227 --> 00:06:38,424
and check each value and date.

68
00:06:38,624 --> 00:06:44,905
For the A1C, look in the Results tab, then the lab reports in Misc, then the progress notes.

69
00:06:45,105 --> 00:06:49,914
Search the notes for A1C, and enter the value with the date it was measured.

70
00:06:50,114 --> 00:06:52,555
Then click Finalize Incomplete.

71
00:06:54,755 --> 00:06:58,281
That's part six, and the end of lesson 4.2.

72
00:06:58,481 --> 00:07:03,717
The patient is enrolled in CCM, and the initial assessment is complete.
